1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
The Forbidden City hides about 13 km of drains underground.
{\fs13}I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,400
600 years of Beijing storms — and it still sheds the rain on its own.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:12,000
First the rain slides into open stone ditches along the courtyards.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Then it drops into covered channels — about 13 km of them, all unseen.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
They feed the Inner Golden Water River and its five marble bridges.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,500
From there it spills out into the 52-metre moat — no pumps anywhere.

7
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,000
About 15 km of old drains — roughly 13 km hidden under your feet.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Genius engineering, or just a clever slope? Tell me I'm wrong below.
